> A delimiter is not an error-correction code

Changing the first bit of0011, the code for three, gives1011, the valid
code for four. The parser accepts it and the value changes silently.
Other changes destroy a terminator and produce an unfinished frame. A
strict parser checks structural validity and representability, not whether
the source values are still correct. External framing, checksums or error
correction would be separate format choices.

The experiment flips each bit of the original ten-value stream once and
runs the native whole-frame decoder. The categories describe this exact
frame and this single-bit substitution model. They establish neither a
universal bound on damaged values nor recovery from arbitrary insertions,
deletions, bursts or arbitrary starting offsets. Overlapping11 patterns
can occur across word boundaries, so treating the next visible11 as an
unconditional original-boundary certificate is unsafe. The original blanket
“at most two codewords” statement is not part of this API's contract.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fibonacci_corruption.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/algorithms/fibonacci_coding.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/exp_golomb.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <cstdint>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto original=dm::algorithms::fibonacci_encode({1,2,3,4,7,10,50,100,1000,100000});std::size_t same=0,changed=0,rejected=0;for(std::size_t i=0;i<original.size();++i){auto mutated=original;mutated[i]=!mutated[i];try{const auto decoded=dm::algorithms::fibonacci_decode(mutated);if(decoded==std::vector<std::uint64_t>{1,2,3,4,7,10,50,100,1000,100000})++same;else ++changed;}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++rejected;}catch(const std::overflow_error&){++rejected;}}
  std::print("Original-frame single-bit flips: tested {}; accepted unchanged {}; accepted changed {}; structurally rejected {}.\n",original.size(),same,changed,rejected);const auto three=dm::algorithms::fibonacci_encode({3});auto four=three;four[0]=!four[0];std::print("Silent valid change: {} -> {}; decoded {} -> {}.\n",dm::algorithms::exp_golomb_bit_string(three),dm::algorithms::exp_golomb_bit_string(four),dm::algorithms::fibonacci_decode(three).front(),dm::algorithms::fibonacci_decode(four).front());std::print("| repeated-one values | flipped bit index | whole-frame unfinished-tail rejection |\n| ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");for(std::size_t n:{4,16,64}){auto b=dm::algorithms::fibonacci_encode(std::vector<std::uint64_t>(n,1));b[2]=false;bool invalid=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::fibonacci_decode(b);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){invalid=true;}std::print("| {} | 2 | {} |\n",n,invalid);if(!invalid)throw std::runtime_error("corruption control failed");}
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();plot.bars({0,1,2},{double(same),double(changed),double(rejected)},"Observed mutations",{37,99,235}).x_tick_labels({"Accepted unchanged","Accepted changed","Rejected frame"}).title("All single-bit flips of the original sample frame").x_label("Native strict whole-frame outcome").y_label("Number of mutations").size(1100,560).save_svg("build/fibonacci_corruption.svg");if(same+changed+rejected!=original.size()||dm::algorithms::fibonacci_decode(four).front()!=4)throw std::runtime_error("mutation census failed");
}
