\caption(Native emission and parsing agree on every word boundary and logical bit count. Exact and failed capture limits and independent ownership execute alongside the measured C=B+2N identity.)
\alttext(A native scatter plot compares actual captured entries with B plus twice N for empty,tiny,original-sample and maximum-value traces. The points lie on the diagonal; printed rows show actual emission and parsing spans.)

> Verification and source

The core now supports the full positive uint64 range, while preserving
69634 frozen records of valid old codewords, decoded values, a1000-value
batch and arbitrary-prefix append, plus all25 lines of original program
stdout. Strict sanitizer tests enumerate17710 small nonadjacent codewords
independently of greedy encoding, test every representable weight boundary,
10000 seeded full-width values and600 variable batches, strict tails,
unsigned value overflow, actual spans, quotas and ownership. An optional
arbitrary-precision Python oracle independently checks23578 encode/decode
results; it is not a report runtime dependency.

A. Apostolico and A. S. Fraenkel,
[Robust Transmission of Unbounded Strings Using Fibonacci Representations](https://docs.lib.purdue.edu/cstech/464/),
Purdue technical report CSD-TR-545, October1985; subsequently IEEE Transactions
on Information Theory33(2),1987,pp.238–245,
[doi:10.1109/TIT.1987.1057284](https://doi.org/10.1109/TIT.1987.1057284),
studies generalized Fibonacci representations and their delimiter structure.
The inspected1985 report distinguishes several representations. This report
specifies datamunge's order-two ascending-weight positive-integer variant
and tests its strict parser directly; it does not infer a universal corruption
recovery guarantee from the paper's title. The repository's existing native
Exp-Golomb APIs supply the comparison lengths and generic bit-text rendering.
